onding to the hundreds digit of 661. This calculation yields 588,000.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 980 + 58,800 + 588,000. Summing these gives a total of 647,780.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '647780', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to multiply 980 by each digit of 661, starting from the ones place.\n\nI'll begin by multiplying 980 by 1, which is the ones digit of 661. This gives me 980.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 980 by 60, which represents the tens digit of 661. This results in 58,800.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 980 by 600, corresponding to the hundreds digit of 661. This calculation yields 588,000.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 980 + 58,800 + 588,000", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 980 and 661?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 980 and 661 step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 980 by the ones place digit (1) of 661:**\n   \\[\n   980 \\times 1 = 980\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 980 by the tens place digit (60) of 661:**\n   \\[\n   980 \\times 60 = 58,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 980 by the hundreds place digit (600) of 661:**\n   \\[\n   980 \\times 600 = 588,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   980 + 58,\\!800 + 588,\\!000 = 647,\\!780\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe final computed product is \\(\\boxed{647,\\!780}\\).", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '649780'}
